      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: There is a serious bug here. In multi-byte FIFO read transactions, `bytes` increases monotonically (0, 1, 2...) while `fifo_head` is simultaneously advanced by `LSM6DSO_FIFO_SAMPLE_SIZE` (7 bytes) every 7 bytes. This results in skipping samples and eventually reading out of bounds.\n\nFor example:\nFirst sample (`bytes \u003d 0..6`): `fifo_head[bytes]` reads `fifo_head_start[0..6]`. At `bytes \u003d 6`, `fifo_head` is advanced by 7.\nSecond sample (`bytes \u003d 7`): `fifo_head[7]` will access `(fifo_head_start + 7)[7] \u003d fifo_head_start[14]`, missing the 2nd sample completely!\n\nYou should be accessing `data-\u003efifo_head[bytes % LSM6DSO_FIFO_SAMPLE_SIZE]` instead.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 223,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 223,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "39504da7aa9def03e88576dd529810265d428d31",
