      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: There is an index counting inconsistency here. In `lsm6dso_emul_read_byte` line 239, you read using `data-\u003ereg[reg + bytes]`, implying `bytes` is 0-indexed. But here you write using `data-\u003ereg[reg + bytes - 1]`, implying `bytes` is 1-indexed. \n\nSince both come from standard Zephyr `i2c_common_emul` callbacks, the `bytes` parameter behavior should be consistent. One of these indexing approaches is likely buggy. If `bytes` is 0-indexed, this code will write to `reg - 1`. If `reg` is 0 and `bytes` is 0, `reg + bytes - 1` becomes -1, which when converted to unsigned (due to `sizeof`) will yield a very large value and falsely trigger the `-ENOTSUP` bounds check blocking legitimate writes to register 0.",
